'Glue F4 and F5 to the top of the wing, then the aft of the upper sides, heat-forming the inward curve and pinning.',
'Bevel the turtledeck supports, glue them to the top inside edges, then the two turtledeck top pieces one at a time.',
'Glue the turtledeck spine on the centreline and the five bulkheads T1–T5.'],
tools:['Upper bulkheads ×3','F4 & F5','Turtledeck supports ×2','Turtledeck tops ×2','Spine','T1–T5','3M 77','Sanding block','Heat gun','Pins & tape'],
tip:'The 1/64" plywood bridge over the rudder servo hole lets the top piece sit flat along the whole spine. Fit the two turtledeck top pieces one at a time so each forms to its own curve.',
check:['Upper and lower meet in a sharp edge','Aft sides curve inward smoothly','Spine straight, five bulkheads square to it','Forward top fitted but not glued at the aft']},
{n:'09',t:'Nose, canopy & tail booms',p:[12,13],intro:'Laminated nosecone and canopy, then the booms that carry the stabilator pivots.',what:[
'Laminate all nosecone and canopy pieces with 3M 77, then glue the nosecone block to the front.',
'Trace the top outline from the template and cut to shape with a long knife or saw.',
