{n:'11',t:'Fuselage top & electronics',p:[17,18],intro:'The hardest part of the build, then the electronics — where ESC placement matters more than most expect.',what:[
'Cut all the bevels in the aft top piece, then cover most of the bottom with packing tape so it cannot wrinkle while heating.',
'Heat-form all the curves, test fitting as you go against the installed turtledeck bulkheads.',
'Trim to a close fit and glue with a light, sandable, gap-filling adhesive. Pin and tape heavily.',
'Fill gaps and build large fillets at the turtledeck and wing junctions with spackling, then sand to shape.',
'Install the receiver aft and the ESC near the middle, with short extensions to motor and nose battery.',
'Locate everything as far forward as possible — the model is tail-heavy. Twist the ESC wires together and tape all wiring flat.',
'Mount the ESC where it gets lots of airflow; inside the inlets is ideal. Cut the shrink wrap back.',
